      "content": "yeah that makes sense. i'm also taking an antidepressant called fluoxetine (prozac) for my anxiety. i read somewhere that mixing things with statins can be tricky, so i've been thinking about maybe just doubling my simvastatin dose for a few days to make sure it's actually working since i've been eating grapefruit. is that a safe way to stay ahead of it, or should i just stick to the regular dose and hope for the best?",
